{# narrative_engine/plot_goal — the step that accomplishes a scheme.
   Asked once per plan by PlotPlanning::Plan, first: what leads up to the
   goal is planned afterwards, backwards from it. The answer is a verb id.
   Receives: mastermind { name, standing }, bio { summary, occupation, ... },
     ambition, scheme, history [string] (steps already taken when a failed
     plan is re-planned, numbered, with how each went; empty at birth),
     options [{ key, line }].
   NOTE: no fenced blocks and no literal braces anywhere in this file. #}
[ state who ]
{{ mastermind.name }}{% if length(mastermind.standing) > 0 %}, {{ mastermind.standing }}{% endif %}.
{{ bio.summary }}
{{ bio.occupation }}
[ end state ]

[ state aims ]
What they are ultimately after: {{ ambition }}
The scheme they mean to carry out: {{ scheme }}
[ end state ]

{% if length(history) > 0 %}[ state history ]
What has happened so far in this scheme:
{% for s in history %}{{ s }}
{% endfor %}[ end state ]

{% endif %}[ question goal choice ]
Which kind of step, once done, is the one that accomplishes the scheme in `aims`? This is the scheme's final step; whatever has to happen before it is decided afterwards. Who or what it involves is also decided afterwards.
[ criteria ]
{% for o in options %}{{ o.key }}: {{ o.line }}
{% endfor %}[ end criteria ]
[ end question ]
